{"title":"2025 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 24\">2025 AMC 10A #24</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2025 AMC 12A #23</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.5_(Cheese,_Goldilocks_Zone)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.5 (Cheese, Goldilocks Zone)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Recursion)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Recursion)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(similar_to_[3])\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (similar to [3])</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:50)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:50)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_(In_2_Mins)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 (In 2 Mins)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3_by_StressedPineapple\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 3 by StressedPineapple</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 4 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Thinking_Feet\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Thinking Feet</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Continuum_Math_(Intuitive_Explanation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Continuum Math (Intuitive Explanation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MadMath_(Easy_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MadMath (Easy Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a positive integer <i>fair</i> if no digit is used more than once, it has no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />s, and no digit is adjacent to two greater digits. For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/1/af1f878102d4ef4719052ec0e61c1bfebe53f366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$196, 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/7/f57ab657668c44460e4e02f552909d0de154ae26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12463$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> are fair, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d623c8170b05a506a1ad797142bd55573675d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1546, 320,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"79\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/e/4de5f886c3ed50bd134dbe4d2e6c22fca80afa81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34321$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> are not. How many fair positive integers are there?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d10a9eb46cdbb1a37b9a92eba1d10a2e4b6ede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 511 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 2584 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 9841 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 17711 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 19682$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"501\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To satisfy the conditions, a fair integer must have no digit be a local minimum. Let's say we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct digits, with each digit being a number from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. To create a fair integer, we begin by placing the largest digit. For the second-largest digit, we can either place this digit to the right or to the left of the string already created. We have these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> options for the third-largest digit, and so on. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/8/66877bd3ddd8dd7995544baee949cc4737866732.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> valid permutations to create a fair integer.\n</p><p>We must also choose which digits will be in the permutation. If you are creating an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-digit long fair integer, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92e926b02fd124589a6ae74e418a72720a5574ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{9}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"41\" height=\"55\" /> ways to pick which digits will be in the number.\n</p><p>Therefore, for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/c/29cff0a6556e813fac0390f12767069a91730380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\{1,2,\\dots, 9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" />, the number of fair integers of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/2/a12ededc3f03a65e075762f9da27893cec04cbd0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{9}{n} \\cdot 2^{n-1}.\\]\" width=\"86\" height=\"53\" />\nSumming over all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/93388fc6940e9592bdde971e04569ccc495c820c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^9{\\binom{9}{n} \\cdot 2^{n-1}}=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\sum_{n=0}^9{\\binom{9}{n}}2^n -1\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left((1+2)^9 -1 \\right) = \\frac{1}{2}(19682) = \\boxed{9841}.\\]\" width=\"623\" height=\"53\" />\nNote that the Binomial Theorem was used to equate\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d99da1d5c23d62fe6bbd15ebf43228c105f7d7da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=0}^9{\\binom{9}{n}}2^n = (1+2)^9.\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"53\" />\n~lprado\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note every fair number will have an increasing string of digits, a maximum digit, then a decreasing string of digits. This is because if it decreases then increases, then the digit in the middle will be less than its adjacent digits.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be the maximum digit. For each number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/82523f7db47c9845b094810522219ed670508345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, we may either place <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, or choose not to include it. Note this process will result in a unique number for every case, as the numbers before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be in increasing order, and the numbers after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be in decreasing order. Therefore, for each number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0dea899ea737ade718bfbfe42e9cd27fbcfa3df3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{n-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"17\" /> cases.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/4/294d0ffe5d11db22b300911d59193ce061071ff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\{1,2,\\cdots9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"121\" height=\"20\" />, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f6c024d38cd43f95fa901e5b2f64811a983a838.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^9 3^{n-1}=\\frac{3^9-1}{3-1}=\\boxed{9841}.\\]\" width=\"215\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p>~SilverRush\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2.5_.28Cheese.2C_Goldilocks_Zone.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.5_(Cheese,_Goldilocks_Zone)\">Solution 2.5 (Cheese, Goldilocks Zone)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.5 (Cheese, Goldilocks Zone)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If you consider options <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> too big, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> too small, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e83b68c968dbcb84eaaa25881d6bd5a57f6ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\text {(C) } 9841}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" /> is your answer.\n</p><p>Also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is twice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is most likely your answer.\n</p><p>- Ameen Patel IrvingtonHighSchoolMathGeeks\n-Edited by TFEA\n</p><p>~Minor edits by Sophia866 and Diamond_427 and hellokindsir and Lunar_paradox\n</p><p>~ WARNING: DO NOT EVER USE! VERY VERY RISKY!\n</p><p>~ Sidenote: You could also notice that the only reasonable answers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and that since every case has a double by flipping it around(making it even) EXCEPT <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> extra cases), meaning the answer has to be odd so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is your answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Recursion.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Recursion)\">Solution 3 (Recursion)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Recursion)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> be the number of fair integers given an arbitrary set of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digits. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest of these digits. Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is either the first or last digit, as if it were any other digit, the two digits surrounding it would both be greater. Then, notice that if the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> slots form a fair number, so does the number when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is appended. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8126a1e168ee181c71714bebf5fcea3f98f6da9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 2f(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />. From here, we may proceed with the calculation in Solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/e/58e83b68c968dbcb84eaaa25881d6bd5a57f6ee9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\text {(C) } 9841}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"80\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ Shadowleafy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any fair integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we write some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> number(s) <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/a/43ae011508e5958e9f51b9fa4fe25961fc1e4c38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\left(\\overline{d_1 d_2 \\ldots d_9}\\right)_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"164\" height=\"25\" /> from left to right as follows:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/0/780fcddd1ec19591cac260789f9dcd0ae8d05735.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is not in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/e/27ee060ce3413dafd2a826c65d643d3ffed64ac5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the to the left of all digits greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />;</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b382d3014102c6162ec7448a97e95fcd87561f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the to the right of all digits greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Note that the fairness ensured one and only one of the above three cases happens. \n</p><p>Now if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is the largest digit in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d09bd8dc83be3b4a1bc205b9cc6fa40b23c7a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> can be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>An example: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/3/b83d6a3651217a2d2e72e3c828c96830aaeba7bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=136852$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4ed9d2c583d3d7dad781736707b9c74399bb96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)=\\overline{121021010}_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"22\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0fa841e7e626db44c23ff9e8e262bce8781c1c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{121021020}_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>It's thus easy to see that there is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-to-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> mapping from all fair integers to all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit base-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> nonzero numbers. Therefore the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/8/a38c470f6b22836b229125d9d34cf2822e4a9765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{3^9-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"54\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~ asops\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28similar_to_.5B3.5D.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(similar_to_[3])\">Solution 5 (similar to [3])</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (similar to [3])\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><b>Lemma:</b> Consider any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digit fair integer, and drop the smallest digit. The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> version of a fair integer should be a fair integer.\n</p><p><b>Proof of the Lemma:</b>\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0ef15285b16f634dbde919b45b97d5ef6a0ba59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{a_1 a_2 a_3 a_4 \\dots a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/8/15823465874e80af38cdc01df3e9ce33ca5ddca7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\leq 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is the integer, then firstly notice that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is the smallest, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must be on either one of the endpoints. If you drop this digit, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/6/1563af4229299f98d624c9a8fedea14d0d377393.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{a_2 a_3 a_4 \\dots a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" /> is an integer. Since adding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to either one of the endpoints is an identity (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> is the smallest), the given integer must be fair as otherwise its <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digit interpretation is not fair. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><b>2025 AMC 12A P23:</b>\n</p><p>From an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> string, we can choose a smaller digit and place it in two ways, the start or end point, and we have the recurrence, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> denotes the number of fair integers given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> digits: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8126a1e168ee181c71714bebf5fcea3f98f6da9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n) = 2f(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>One can simply bash the recurrence from here to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d7232241193da1133e7c72c2b2674c6ac3403514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{9841}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"49\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_.28Logical.2C_Good_Editing.2C_.7E1:50.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_FormulaFocus_(Logical,_Good_Editing,_~1:50)\">Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:50)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by FormulaFocus (Logical, Good Editing, ~1:50)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/mZlBUqiRXzY\">https://www.youtube.com/shorts/mZlBUqiRXzY</a>\n</p><p>~Ebai\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Quick_and_Easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Quick_and_Easy)\">Video Solution(Quick and Easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Quick and Easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g_JiDAaYRHs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g_JiDAaYRHs</a>\n~Sigma_Bob\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_1_.28In_2_Mins.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_(In_2_Mins)\">Video Solution 1 (In 2 Mins)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 (In 2 Mins)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hYZkrBtIFvI?si=dMOaGsXSpxYV17PO\">https://youtu.be/hYZkrBtIFvI?si=dMOaGsXSpxYV17PO</a> ~ Pi Academy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2_by_OmegaLearn.org\">Video Solution 2 by OmegaLearn.org</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit sectio